cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Mithril snarkification — a SNARK-friendly variant of the
  Mithril multi-signature protocol
message: >-
  If you use this software or the design it proposes, please
  cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jia
    family-names: Liu
    affiliation: Input Output Global
  - given-names: Raphael
    family-names: Toledo
    affiliation: Input Output Global
repository-code: 'https://github.com/input-output-hk/mithril-circuits'
abstract: >-
  A research prototype that proposes and implements a
  SNARK-friendly redesign of the Mithril stake-based
  multi-signature protocol (Cardano), together with a
  recursive (IVC) proof system that folds an unbounded chain
  of certificates across epochs into a constant-size proof
  plus a KZG accumulator.
keywords:
  - Mithril
  - Cardano
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - SNARK
  - PLONK
  - incrementally verifiable computation
  - multi-signature
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-04-01'
